### N7c lock shapes: an owner-less lock (old and fresh), a reused pid, a reused ENGINE GROUP id.
owner-less lock, seconds old: rc=6 (REFUSED — another run holds the lock /private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-DevMASTER-WEDNESDAY/)
owner-less lock, old: rc=6 (REFUSED — STALE lock at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-Dev)
   clear: rc=0
live pid, different start time (pid reuse): rc=6 (REFUSED — STALE lock at /private/tmp/claude-501/-Volumes-Dev)
   clear: rc=0
dead holder, engine_pgid = the group of an UNRELATED live process (a reused group id, e.g. after a reboot): clear rc=6 (nas-backup: REFUSED — the holder (pid 999999) is gone but 4 copy-engine process(es) of this seat are STILL RUNNING (65856 /bin/zsh -c source /Users/ka)
